prompt:
{
  "public_instructions": "You translate natural-language access-control requirements into Cedar policies using the supplied schema. Cedar denies by default. An applicable forbid overrides every permit. Guard optional attributes with has before reading them. Preserve the schema's entity, set, and attribute types. Use only the supplied task information. Do not use tools, files, search, additional model calls, or external feedback. Produce a single final answer as a JSON object with exactly one field, policy, whose value is the complete Cedar policy text. Do not include explanations or Markdown fences.
",
  "harness": {
    "instruction_blocks": [
      "Translate the access-control requirements into a complete Cedar policy set. Identify each action, eligible principal, resource type, required condition, prohibition, and exception. Use only entity types, attributes, actions, and representations supported by the schema. Implement the stated permissions and restrictions together.",
      "Before answering, check the policy mentally for both unauthorized permissions and missing required permissions. Keep distinct action rules separate when their conditions differ. Apply exceptions only to the restriction they qualify. Return one final policy set."
    ],
    "input_order": [
      "requirements",
      "schema"
    ],
    "checklist": [
      "Every required action is covered.",
      "Role, ownership, membership, and context conditions follow the requirements.",
      "Prohibitions and exceptions compose correctly.",
      "Optional attribute reads are guarded and Cedar syntax is valid."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": "The system manages clear-to-close approval and fund disbursement for real-estate escrow files.

The people involved are escrow officers, senior escrow officers, escrow managers, title officers, and auditors. One person may hold both the escrow officer and senior escrow officer roles at the same time, or both the senior escrow officer and escrow manager roles at the same time.

The resources are escrow files and disbursements. Every escrow file records its escrow officer, its disbursement tier, the amount held, the number of payees, its file code, its region, its parties, its lien status, whether its title has been cleared, its status, and its closing date. Every disbursement records its escrow file, who authorized it, its amount, and when it was wired.

Each request carries the current time, whether it comes from the corporate network, whether dual control has been confirmed, and whether a settlement emergency has been declared.

An escrow officer may open an escrow file, and a title officer or an escrow manager may then approve that file clear to close.

An escrow officer who opened a file and who also serves as the approving title officer or escrow manager may not approve that same file clear to close, while a title officer or escrow manager who did not open the file may approve it.

A file may be approved clear to close only when its title has been cleared of encumbrances, while a request to approve a file whose title still carries encumbrances must be refused.

An auditor may only view the audit log and must not approve any file clear to close.

A request by a title officer to approve a clear to close for a file that trips none of the prohibitions above must be able to succeed.",
  "schema": "entity Person {
    isEscrowOfficer: Bool,
    isSeniorEscrowOfficer: Bool,
    isEscrowManager: Bool,
    isTitleOfficer: Bool,
    isAuditor: Bool,
};

entity EscrowFile {
    escrowOfficer: Person,
    openedBy: Person,
    disbursementTier: String,
    amountHeld: decimal,
    numberOfPayees: Long,
    fileCode: String,
    region: String,
    parties: Set<String>,
    lienStatus: String,
    titleCleared: Bool,
    status: String,
    closingDate: datetime,
};

entity Disbursement {
    escrowFile: EscrowFile,
    authorizedBy: Person,
    amount: decimal,
    wiredAt: datetime,
};

entity AuditLog;

action openEscrowFile appliesTo {
    principal: [Person],
    resource: [EscrowFile],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        fromCorporateNetwork: Bool,
        dualControlConfirmed: Bool,
        settlementEmergencyDeclared: Bool,
    },
};

action approveClearToClose appliesTo {
    principal: [Person],
    resource: [EscrowFile],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        fromCorporateNetwork: Bool,
        dualControlConfirmed: Bool,
        settlementEmergencyDeclared: Bool,
    },
};

action viewAuditLog appliesTo {
    principal: [Person],
    resource: [AuditLog],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        fromCorporateNetwork: Bool,
        dualControlConfirmed: Bool,
        settlementEmergencyDeclared: Bool,
    },
};
"
}
